message: If you use this repository, please cite this reproduction bundle and the
  accompanying preprint.
title: Reproduction Bundle for 'Diverging paths to dark-matter discovery'
type: software
version: 3.0.0
date-released: '2026-10-09'
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/SALLZEN/dark-matter-plurality
url: https://github.com/SALLZEN/dark-matter-plurality
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.20241725
authors:
- family-names: Allzén
  given-names: Simon
  affiliation: Stockholm University; University of Amsterdam
abstract: Code and data reproduction bundle for the preprint “Diverging paths to dark-matter
  discovery”. Includes the frozen ADS snapshot, six-stage statistical pipeline, validation
  and robustness materials, network ontology and analysis code, frozen network events
  and metrics, graph exports and saved layouts, and five main and five supplementary
  figure assets. The analysis cutoff is 2025. Manuscript source and the compiled preprint
  are maintained separately. Network outputs and presentations are preserved as historical
  artifacts; exact recreation of them by the current network code is not claimed.
keywords:
- dark matter
- bibliometrics
- arXiv
- NASA ADS
- astroparticle physics
- reproducibility
